From 22e8c26c40656aa69afa99c0878c81bac68ad7c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicole Muzzin <nicks@fuckin.email>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 05:41:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] script: a shadow root's document and window follow its host
 on adopt

ShadowRoot kept the Document and Window it was created with in its own
fields, and DocumentOrShadowRoot kept a Window, while adopting the host
only updated the node document. After document.adoptNode() of a host
created in another document (for example a createHTMLDocument() one),
adoptedStyleSheets rejected sheets constructed in the new document with
NotAllowedError, elementFromPoint/elementsFromPoint returned nothing
because the old document has no browsing context, and new shadow-tree
stylesheets were registered against the old document.

Per DOM, adopting sets the node document of every shadow-including
descendant, shadow roots included, so ShadowRoot now reads its document
and window from its node document and the stored copies are gone. The
DocumentOrShadowRoot helpers take the window from the node they act on,
which also makes activeElement use this's node document as the HTML
spec says instead of the window's active document.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
